@startuml ModeActivityDiagram
title Choosing and switching modes (Duke + the two CLIs)

start
:Load saved records (Storage);
:Print "Choose a mode: baker or customer";
repeat
  :Read one line;
  if (Valid mode?\nbaker/1/b or customer/2/c) then (yes)
  else (no)
    :Print "Error: Choose a mode...";
  endif
repeat while (No valid mode yet?)

repeat
  if (Current mode?) then (BAKER)
    :Run BakerCli loop;
  else (CUSTOMER)
    :Run CustomerCli loop;
  endif
  note right
    Inside a CLI loop, each command is
    parsed, executed, printed, and (if it
    changed anything) saved. Invalid input
    prints an Error and the loop continues.
  end note
repeat while (User typed "mode ..."\n(returned next mode)) is (switch)
-> user typed bye, or input ended;
stop
@enduml
